    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d79">

                <pb facs="0150" n="70" sameAs="frus:frus1901/pg70"/>

                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Wu.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1901-12-03"><hi rendition="#italic">December 3,
                        1901</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 187.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to acknowledge the receipt
                    of your note No. 214, of the 28th ultimo, requesting that permission be granted
                    to the Chinese student, Tong Tseng, whose case is described in your note, to
                    land at Honolulu, to which place he goes for the purpose of pursuing an
                    educational course.</p>
                <p>In reply I have the honor to inform you that I have sent a copy of your note to
                    the Secretary of the Treasury for his information, and have commended the case
                    to his consideration.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
